  "summary": "Malicious code in @vault-v2-reallocation-bot/config (npm)",
  "details": "The package manifest declares a dependency on its own package name resolved from a non-registry plain-HTTP host: dependencies[\"@vault-v2-reallocation-bot/config\"] = \"hxxp://pack[.]nppacks[.]com/npm/@vault-v2-reallocation-bot/config\" (also in devDependencies). Installing the package redirects dependency resolution to that external host over unencrypted HTTP, allowing the host to serve arbitrary code as the dependency. The bundled index.js is a copy of the babel-plugin-transform-define Babel plugin; the supply-chain risk is the external self-dependency URL, not the shipped code.",
